+function codexView(){if(!codexUnlocked())return `${pageHead('REFERENCE LIBRARY · ACCESS LOCKED','DNA Codex','A curated field guide to DNA, genomes, and the methods used to study them.')}<section class="card codex-lock"><div class="codex-lock-icon">⌬</div><div class="eyebrow">CODEX SEALED</div><h2>${S.plate.length?'Complete a research success to unlock the Codex':'Place a biological source on the observatory plate'}</h2><p>The Codex becomes available when a source is present on the plate and at least one lab protocol or genome-sequencing run succeeds. Curated reference material remains hidden until then.</p><div class="codex-unlock-steps"><span class="${S.plate.length?'complete':''}">01 · SOURCE ON PLATE</span><span class="${S.researchSuccesses?'complete':''}">02 · RESEARCH SUCCESS</span></div><button class="action-button primary" data-view="cell">Open cell observatory →</button></section>`;return `${pageHead('REFERENCE LIBRARY · ${DNA_CODEX.length} FIELD NOTES','DNA Codex','A curated educational guide to what is known about DNA—and how evidence is interpreted.',`<span class="tag green">UNLOCKED · ${S.researchSuccesses} SUCCESS${S.researchSuccesses===1?'':'ES'}</span>`)}<section class="card codex-intro"><div><div class="eyebrow">SCOPE &amp; CONTEXT</div><h2>DNA is a molecule, not a complete explanation.</h2><p>This living reference summarizes established concepts across molecular biology, genomics, evolution, and research practice. It is intentionally curated—not an exhaustive database of every sequence, organism, or discovery. Scientific knowledge changes, and model readouts elsewhere in GENESIS are educational proxies rather than real biological measurements.</p></div><div class="codex-stat"><strong>${DNA_CODEX.length}</strong><span>TOPIC GUIDES</span><small>${S.plate.length} source cells present</small></div></section><div class="codex-grid">${DNA_CODEX.map((entry,i)=>`<article class="card codex-entry"><div class="codex-entry-top"><span class="codex-index">${Stri